    '<summary><span class="gi">' + brand("alexa") + "</span><div><b>Connect an Alexa skill</b>" +
    "<small>A custom skill that calls the app's own HTTPS endpoint and draws on Echo Show screens</small></div>" + icon("chevron", "chev") + "</summary>" +
    '<div class="gbody">' +
    '<a class="btn" href="https://developer.amazon.com/alexa/console/ask" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">' + icon("out") + "Open Alexa Developer Console</a>" +
    skillNotes +
    '<ol class="steps">' +
    '<li class="warn" data-if="notunnel" hidden>This container is not on ' + chip(null, "localinfra_tunnel") +
    ", so Alexa can't reach it. Publish it on Cloudflare first.</li>" +
    '<li>The app must answer on its public address: follow <a href="#guide-cloudflare">Publish an app on Cloudflare</a> first.' +
    '<span class="note">If Bot Fight Mode or a WAF rule is on for the zone, let the skill endpoint through: Alexa calls from AWS.</span></li>' +
    "<li><b>Create Skill</b>: name, primary locale (the app's language, e.g. Portuguese (BR)), type <b>Other → Custom</b>, hosting <b>Provision your own</b>, template <b>Start from scratch</b>." +
    '<span class="note">Apps with an alexa/ask-resources.json (sports-cal, brain-gym) can skip steps 2 to 6: <kbd>npx ask-cli deploy</kbd> from alexa/, after replacing SEU-DOMINIO in skill-package/skill.json.</span></li>' +
    "<li><b>Endpoint</b> → HTTPS, Default Region " + chip("alexa", "https://myapp.example.com/api/alexa") +
