    "<li><b>Interfaces</b> → turn on <b>Alexa Presentation Language</b>, Save, then <b>Build skill</b> again." +
    '<span class="note">This is what puts the skill on the screen: without it Alexa never tells the app the device has one, and an Echo Show only shows the spoken text. ' +
    "Devices without a screen keep getting the full spoken answers.</span></li>" +
    "<li><b>Permissions</b>: the ones the app's <kbd>skill.json</kbd> lists (in the box above: Reminders, Notifications, Timers)." +
    '<span class="note">The ASK CLI turns on interfaces and permissions by itself.</span></li>' +
    "<li>Copy the skill id (Alexa Skills list → <b>Copy Skill ID</b>) into the app's <kbd>.env</kbd> and run <kbd>./deploy.sh</kbd> " +
    chip(null, "ALEXA_SKILL_ID=amzn1.ask.skill.") +
    '<span class="note">The app then answers only this skill. Until it is set, sports-cal and my-recipes refuse every request.</span></li>' +
    "<li><b>Test</b> tab → <i>Skill testing is enabled in</i> " + chip(null, "Development") +
    '<span class="note">Tick <b>Device Display</b> in the simulator to see the screens, then try it on an Echo Show: the screen stays up while the skill is open, and its mute button silences that device. ' +
    "Any Echo signed in to the same Amazon account gets the skill too. It stays private unless submitted for certification. " +
    "Reminders or Timers must also be allowed once: in the Alexa app (Skills → Your Skills → Dev) or by voice when the Echo asks.</span></li>" +
    "</ol></div></details>";

  return (
    '<div class="ghead"><h2>Guides</h2>' +
    '<label class="field"><span>App</span><select id="g-app">' + options + "</select></label>" +
    '<label class="field"><span>Domain</span><input id="g-domain" placeholder="example.com" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" value="' +
    escape(domain) + '"></label></div>' +
    cloudflare + google + alexa
  );
}

// Client side: refresh the live part, map highlighting, guide values, copy buttons
const SCRIPT = [
  "(function () {",
  "  var live = document.getElementById('live'), beat = document.getElementById('beat'), stamp = document.getElementById('stamp');",
  "  function now() { stamp.textContent = 'updated ' + new Date().toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', second: '2-digit' }); }",
  "  function refresh() {",
  "    if (document.hidden) return;",
  "    fetch('live', { cache: 'no-store' }).then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status); return r.text(); })",
  "      .then(function (html) { live.innerHTML = html; stamps(); ranges(); beat.classList.remove('off'); now(); })",
  "      .catch(function () { beat.classList.add('off'); stamp.textContent = 'offline, retrying'; });",
  "  }",
